>Section</b> <b>126</b>  of the <b>Electricity</b> ... <b>unauthorised</b> <b>use</b> of <b>electricity</b>. There is absolutely no reference to\n            such <b>unauthorised</b> <b>use</b> being in excess of the contract demand.\n            <b>Unauthorised</b> <b>use</b>", "docsize": 44479, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Kerala High Court", "author": "A K Nambiar", "authorEncoded": "a-k-nambiar"}, {"tid": 41279607, "catids": null, "doctype": 1024, "publishdate": "2024-08-21", "authorid": null, "bench": null, "title": "B.P.S. Ispat Udyog And Another vs Punjab State Power Corporation Ltd. ... on 21 August, 2024", "numcites": 3, "numcitedby": 0, "headline": "connection A/c\n       LK 02/00026 amounts to <b>unauthorised</b> <b>use</b> of <b>electricity</b> as per\n        <b>Section</b> <b>126</b> (6) (b) (v)  of the <b>Electricity</b> ... different\n          premises. Thus <b>use</b> of one connection for two differen\n                                                       different premises\n          amounted to <b>unauthorised</b> <b>use</b> of <b>electricity</b> as per  <b>Section</b> <b>126</b>", "docsize": 55261, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Punjab-Haryana High Court"}, {"tid": 125946405, "catids": [1, 42], "doctype": 1017, "publishdate": "2015-02-23", "authorid": 793, "bench": [793], "title": "Paschim Gujarat Vij Co Ltd vs <b>Electrical</b> Inspector & on 23 February, 2015", "numcites": 5, "numcitedby": 0, "headline": "<b>unauthorised</b>\u00a0<b>use</b>\u00a0of\u00a0<b>electricity</b>.\u00a0What\u00a0constitutes\u00a0\n\n&quot;<b>unauthorised</b>\u00a0<b>use</b>\u00a0of\u00a0<b>electricity</b>&quot;\u00a0has\u00a0been\u00a0adequately\u00a0\n\nexplained \u00a0 and \u00a0 illustrated \u00a0 in \u00a0 the \u00a0 explanations \u00a0 to\u00a0\n\n <b>Section</b>\u00a0<b>126</b> ... bills \u00a0 for\u00a0\n\nconsumption\u00a0of\u00a0<b>electricity</b>,\u00a0but\u00a0when\u00a0an\u00a0<b>unauthorised</b>\u00a0\n\n<b>use</b>\u00a0of\u00a0<b>electricity</b>\u00a0is\u00a0discovered,\u00a0sub\u00ad<b>section</b>\u00a0(6)\u00a0of\u00a0\n\n <b>Section</b>\u00a0<b>126</b> \u00a0comes\u00a0into\u00a0play", "docsize": 41027, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Gujarat High Court", "author": "A Kumari", "authorEncoded": "a-kumari"}, {"tid": 190140835, "catids": null, "doctype": 1004, "publishdate": "2026-03-04", "authorid": null, "bench": null, "title": "Maharashtra <b>Electricity</b> Distribution ... vs Pankaj Trilokchand Pande on 4 March, 2026", "numcites": 3, "numcitedby": 0, "headline": "<b>Section</b> <b>126</b> of\n           the 2003 Act.\n \n            2.      The expression &quot;<b>unauthorised</b> <b>use</b> of <b>electricity</b>\n           means&quot; as appearing in a <b>Section</b> <b>126</b> ... <b>use</b> of <b>electricity</b> which is not permissible and beyond the\ncontract demand amounts to <b>unauthorised</b> <b>use</b> of <b>electricity</b> and\nthe blame contemplated under <b>Section</b> <b>126</b>", "docsize": 29616, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Bombay High Court"}, {"tid": 189191529, "catids": null, "doctype": 1006, "publishdate": "2021-11-16", "authorid": 573, "bench": [573], "title": "M/S. B. Choudhury & Co vs Cesc Limited And Others on 16 November, 2021", "numcites": 5, "numcitedby": 0, "headline": "<b>unauthorised</b>\n\n      <b>use</b> of <b>electricity</b>. The instances of &quot;<b>unauthorised</b> <b>use</b> of <b>electricity</b>&quot;\n\n      have been clearly defined in Explanation (b) of  <b>Section</b> <b>126</b> ... person\n\n      indulging in <b>unauthorised</b> <b>use</b> of <b>electricity</b> or any other person\n\n      benefited by such <b>use</b>.\n\n21.   Sub-<b>section</b> (2) of  <b>Section</b> <b>126</b>  contemplates service", "docsize": 22313, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Calcutta High Court (Appellete Side)", "author": "S Bhattacharyya", "authorEncoded": "s-bhattacharyya"}, {"tid": 137441590, "catids": null, "doctype": 1013, "publishdate": "2014-01-13", "authorid": 1116, "bench": [1116], "title": "Thomas Mathew vs Kerala State <b>Electricity</b> Board on 13 January, 2014", "numcites": 4, "numcitedby": 0, "headline": "<b>section</b> <b>126</b>(6)(b)  of the\n\n<b>Electricity</b> Act 2003.      Illustrations of &quot;<b>unauthorised</b> <b>use</b> of\n\n<b>electricity</b>&quot; enumerated therein specifies that, usage of <b>electricity</b> ... held that <b>unauthorised</b>\n\n<b>use</b> of <b>electricity</b> cannot be restricted to the illustrative\n\nexplanations contained in  <b>section</b> <b>126</b> .        <b>Unauthorised</b> <b>use</b> of\n\n<b>electricity</b> itself is an expression", "docsize": 17953, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Kerala High Court", "author": "C V Rehim", "authorEncoded": "c-v-rehim"}, {"tid": 57637994, "catids": null, "doctype": 1013, "publishdate": "2005-10-28", "authorid": null, "bench": null, "title": "M/S.Aamir Ice & Cold Storage vs Kerala Stateelectricity Board on 28 October, 2005", "numcites": 5, "numcitedby": 0, "headline": "consequences.        <b>Unauthorised</b> <b>use</b>   of   <b>electricity</b>    as\n\f\n W.P.(c) No.17656/2008            -8- \n\n\nenumerated in the Explanations to sub <b>section</b> (6) of  <b>Section</b>\n\n<b>126</b>  includes ... <b>unauthorised</b> <b>use</b> of <b>electricity</b>.\n\nWithout there being any proper and convincing materials\n\navailable to arrive at a conclusion regarding <b>unauthorised</b>\n\n<b>use</b> of <b>electricity</b> imposition", "docsize": 19204, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Kerala High Court"}, {"tid": 176250265, "catids": null, "doctype": 1013, "publishdate": "2005-10-28", "authorid": null, "bench": null, "title": "M/S.Aamir Ice And Cold Storage vs Kerala State <b>Electricity</b> Board on 28 October, 2005", "numcites": 5, "numcitedby": 0, "headline": "consequences.        <b>Unauthorised</b> <b>use</b>   of   <b>electricity</b>    as\n\f\n W.P.(c) No.17656/2008            -8- \n\n\nenumerated in the Explanations to sub <b>section</b> (6) of  <b>Section</b>\n\n<b>126</b>  includes ... <b>unauthorised</b> <b>use</b> of <b>electricity</b>.\n\nWithout there being any proper and convincing materials\n\navailable to arrive at a conclusion regarding <b>unauthorised</b>\n\n<b>use</b> of <b>electricity</b> imposition", "docsize": 19013, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Kerala High Court"}, {"tid": 50430785, "catids": null, "doctype": 1013, "publishdate": "2005-10-28", "authorid": null, "bench": null, "title": "M/S.Aamir Ice & Cold Storage vs Kerala Stateelectricity Boar on 28 October, 2005", "numcites": 5, "numcitedby": 0, "headline": "consequences.        <b>Unauthorised</b> <b>use</b>   of   <b>electricity</b>    as\n\f\n W.P.(c) No.17656/2008            -8- \n\n\nenumerated in the Explanations to sub <b>section</b> (6) of  <b>Section</b>\n\n<b>126</b>  includes ... <b>unauthorised</b> <b>use</b> of <b>electricity</b>.\n\nWithout there being any proper and convincing materials\n\navailable to arrive at a conclusion regarding <b>unauthorised</b>\n\n<b>use</b> of <b>electricity</b> imposition", "docsize": 19202, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Kerala High Court"}], "found": "111 - 120 of 884", "encodedformInput": "%22section%20126%22%20electricity%20%22unauthorised%20use%22%20doctypes%3Ahighcourts"}